PN,31806
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1785858502
OL,3,CNew heat health alerts issued with
OL,4,Chighs of 35C forecast in some areas
OL,6,FPolly Ashmore, of the UKHSA, said:
OL,7,F"Periods of hot weather can result in
OL,8,Fserious health outcomes, especially
OL,9,Ffor older adults, and it is therefore
OL,10,Fimportant that everyone takes sensible
OL,11,Fprecautions while enjoying the sun.
OL,13,F"We are urging health and social care
OL,14,Fservices in affected regions to ensure
OL,15,Fthey are prepared, and reminding
OL,16,Fpeople to look out for elderly
OL,17,Frelatives, neighbours and those with
OL,18,Funderlying health conditions, making
OL,19,Fsure they are aware of the forecast
OL,20,Fand following the necessary advice.
OL,26,@oD@AOUuD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31807
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1785858502
OL,3,CNew heat health alerts issued with
OL,4,Chighs of 35C forecast in some areas
OL,6,F"Simple steps such as staying
OL,7,Fhydrated, avoiding the sun during the
OL,8,Fhottest part of the day, and keeping
OL,9,Fyour home cool are some of the key
OL,10,Fways to help keep yourself and others
OL,11,Fsafe during periods of hot weather."
OL,13,FAngelo Makri, of the Alzheimer's
OL,14,FSociety, warned that high temperatures
OL,15,F"can pose serious risks for people
OL,16,Fliving with dementia if they are not
OL,17,Fsupported to stay cool and hydrated".
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@dO]wD@AOUyD@dO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,319,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31808
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F318A1785858502
OL,3,CNew heat health alerts issued with
OL,4,Chighs of 35C forecast in some areas
OL,6,F"People with dementia may not always
OL,7,Frecognise when they need a drink or
OL,8,Fwear suitable clothing, which can
OL,9,Fincrease the risk of dehydration and
OL,10,Fheat-related illness," he added.
